    "result_text": "I added `require_setting(key)` to `hc/front/decorators.py`. I haven't run it or any tests.\n\nViews under `hc/integrations/` already import it from there and use it, for example `@require_setting(\"WEBHOOKS_ENABLED\")` and `@require_setting(\"SIGNAL_CLI_SOCKET\")`. The file had the imports but no definition, so I wrote the missing function instead of a new decorator.\n\nIt returns a 404 (`HttpResponseNotFound`) when `getattr(settings, key, None)` is falsy. Otherwise it calls the view as normal. Because it checks truthiness, it works for boolean flags like `WEBHOOKS_ENABLED` and for settings that hold a value, like `PUSHOVER_API_TOKEN`.\n\nI also added `HttpResponseNotFound` to the `django.http` import."
